imx8mp: give the on-board eMMC controller (uSDHC3) to the secure world

OP-TEE drives uSDHC3 from the secure world for its RPMB storage and DMAs
RPMB frames straight into its own (TZASC-protected) memory. With the
default CSU setting the controller is a non-secure bus master, so every
such DMA is rejected once OP-TEE has locked the TZASC regions. Make the
master secure, and while at it restrict the controller's registers to the
secure world: U-Boot and Linux have the node disabled in their device
trees and never touch it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board configuration for the TEE-owned eMMC]

--- a/plat/imx/imx8m/imx8mp/imx8mp_bl31_setup.c	2026-09-15 11:13:15.273287873 +0000
+++ b/plat/imx/imx8m/imx8mp/imx8mp_bl31_setup.c	2026-09-15 11:13:15.301287784 +0000
@@ -155,6 +155,8 @@
 	CSU_CSLx(CSU_CSL_RDC, CSU_SEC_LEVEL_3, LOCKED),
 	CSU_CSLx(CSU_CSL_TZASC, CSU_SEC_LEVEL_5, LOCKED),
 	CSU_CSLx(CSU_CSL_CSU, CSU_SEC_LEVEL_5, LOCKED),
+	/* uSDHC3 registers: secure world only (OP-TEE owns the eMMC) */
+	CSU_CSLx(CSU_CSL_uSDHC3, CSU_SEC_LEVEL_4, LOCKED),
 
 	/* master HP0~1 */
 
@@ -168,7 +170,8 @@
 	CSU_SA(CSU_SA_ENET1, NON_SEC_ACCESS, LOCKED),
 	CSU_SA(CSU_SA_USDHC1, NON_SEC_ACCESS, LOCKED),
 	CSU_SA(CSU_SA_USDHC2, NON_SEC_ACCESS, LOCKED),
-	CSU_SA(CSU_SA_USDHC3, NON_SEC_ACCESS, LOCKED),
+	/* uSDHC3 (on-board eMMC) DMAs into OP-TEE memory: secure master */
+	CSU_SA(CSU_SA_USDHC3, SEC_ACCESS, LOCKED),
 	CSU_SA(CSU_SA_HUGO, NON_SEC_ACCESS, LOCKED),
 	CSU_SA(CSU_SA_DAP, NON_SEC_ACCESS, LOCKED),
 	CSU_SA(CSU_SA_SDMA2, NON_SEC_ACCESS, LOCKED),
